Against Famine any 1-turn food will do.  A stack of
lumps of royal jelly are best because they are 100
nutrition points each while K-rations are 40.  Eggs
are 80 so one egg is worth 2 K-rations.

The reason for K-rations is you end up with a bunch
of them in most games.  Other 1-turn foods are less
common.  You'll generally eat all of your royal
jelly and most of the other random food items.  With
a stack of K-rations the advantage is it only takes
one item slot.  So there isn't much fumbling about
for what to eat.  Save the common K-rations and the
choice is easy.

Regular food rations are a bad choice because they
take 3 turns.  Lembas rations are the best nutrition
per weight, so if you want to avoid loading they are
best.  But when facing Famine there is more than
just weight ratio.  You have 1 turn to eat and continue
the battle or you could die.


